WEBVTT

00:00:07.000 --> 00:00:09.940
This is the story of one app.

00:00:09.940 --> 00:00:16.530
From a no, to a launch, to a binder
for everyone you call family.

00:00:34.000 --> 00:00:37.513
Some weeks I'm the mom, the daughter,

00:00:37.513 --> 00:00:41.500
and the one who knows where everything is.

00:00:41.500 --> 00:00:45.412
My dad's insurance. The kids' passports.

00:00:45.412 --> 00:00:48.052
And Sam's car registration,

00:00:48.052 --> 00:00:53.920
because he's in Lisbon for a
year and I'm the one he trusts.

00:01:06.000 --> 00:01:09.361
We wanted to build something for her.

00:01:09.361 --> 00:01:13.357
But first, we had to
fail at something else.

00:01:15.000 --> 00:01:18.099
Our first app was turned down twice.

00:01:18.099 --> 00:01:21.887
It wasn't different
enough. Apple was right.

00:01:30.000 --> 00:01:36.087
So we stopped resubmitting and held
on to the one thing that was good.

00:01:46.000 --> 00:01:49.478
On the twenty-first of
September, we started again.

00:01:55.000 --> 00:02:01.522
Before we had one idea, we built the
filter that every idea had to pass.

00:02:02.000 --> 00:02:03.505
Useful for years.

00:02:03.505 --> 00:02:06.782
Not something the phone already does.

00:02:06.782 --> 00:02:11.121
Private by design. Buildable
in weeks, not years.

00:02:11.121 --> 00:02:13.600
And a business from day one.

00:02:30.500 --> 00:02:33.318
One idea made it through all five.

00:02:33.318 --> 00:02:38.291
We started with the hardest
version: looking after a parent.

00:02:50.000 --> 00:02:51.739
Next, we stopped guessing.

00:02:54.000 --> 00:02:59.328
We searched the store like a
tired person at eleven at night.

00:02:59.328 --> 00:03:01.860
We read the one-star reviews.

00:03:01.860 --> 00:03:07.712
And every form and rule in the app
comes from whoever publishes it.

00:03:07.712 --> 00:03:09.983
States, Medicare, the FTC.

00:03:38.000 --> 00:03:40.127
Six building blocks.

00:03:40.127 --> 00:03:44.487
Most of the app is one of them, or a mix.

00:03:55.000 --> 00:03:59.029
For a few days it was called On Behalf.

00:03:59.029 --> 00:04:01.922
Then we found a better word.

00:04:02.000 --> 00:04:04.999
Provisum. Latin for provided for.

00:04:04.999 --> 00:04:08.452
What you want everyone you love to be.

00:04:12.000 --> 00:04:13.268
Then the look.

00:04:13.268 --> 00:04:17.617
Calm, because people open
this app on hard days.

00:04:39.000 --> 00:04:42.944
Every screen was checked
at the biggest text sizes.

00:04:42.944 --> 00:04:47.661
When something broke, we redesigned
the screen, not the text.

00:04:50.000 --> 00:04:53.756
Native Swift, for iPhone,
Apple Watch and widgets.

00:04:53.756 --> 00:04:55.183
Nothing in between.

00:05:08.000 --> 00:05:12.951
Everything belongs to a binder,
and a binder belongs to a person:

00:05:12.951 --> 00:05:18.435
your dad, your daughter, yourself,
your partner, a friend, even the dog.

00:05:18.500 --> 00:05:21.926
Every date from every source joins one

00:05:21.926 --> 00:05:25.533
list and gets the reminder that fits it.

00:05:25.533 --> 00:05:29.230
Passports get nine, six and three months.

00:05:29.230 --> 00:05:33.648
A bill gets a nudge three
days out, and that day.

00:05:34.000 --> 00:05:36.887
No account. Nothing is collected.

00:05:36.887 --> 00:05:41.523
Your data lives on your
phone and in your own iCloud.

00:05:41.523 --> 00:05:45.635
Sharing goes straight to
the people you invite.

00:05:46.000 --> 00:05:51.217
The emergency card is encrypted on
your iPhone before it goes anywhere.

00:05:54.000 --> 00:06:00.087
We carried the engine over from our first
app, and rebuilt everything around it.

00:06:05.000 --> 00:06:07.174
And App Review said yes.

00:06:20.000 --> 00:06:24.504
We launched in the United States,
where Veyago does business,

00:06:24.504 --> 00:06:27.826
with its states' forms
and Medicare built in.

00:06:31.000 --> 00:06:34.738
On day one we got the price wrong.

00:06:34.738 --> 00:06:37.487
The next day we fixed it.

00:06:40.500 --> 00:06:46.152
Then we looked at what we'd
built, and at who we'd left out.

00:06:50.000 --> 00:06:53.000
It was never only my dad.

00:06:56.000 --> 00:06:59.377
Version one was a binder for a parent.

00:06:59.377 --> 00:07:02.487
Nobody looks after just one person.

00:07:24.000 --> 00:07:28.458
Sam's car, Dad's medications,
the kids' passports.

00:07:28.458 --> 00:07:30.420
Same place. Same calm.

00:07:58.000 --> 00:08:01.287
And the biggest change: no more forms.

00:08:01.287 --> 00:08:04.487
Provisum asks one question at a time.

00:08:35.500 --> 00:08:40.615
Every person gets the documents,
dates and packets that fit them.

00:08:40.615 --> 00:08:43.291
A child's binder isn't a parent's.

00:08:58.000 --> 00:08:59.304
Everything we drew.

00:09:00.000 --> 00:09:03.443
Built natively. Tested at every text size.

00:09:04.000 --> 00:09:06.844
And it's all on my phone.

00:09:06.844 --> 00:09:09.460
Not on anyone's server.

00:09:44.000 --> 00:09:47.166
Provisum. It's Latin for provided for.

00:09:47.166 --> 00:09:49.583
For everyone you call family.
